  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Echohydrology, IWRM, Education and Culture for a Water Secure North East Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water security, in terms of both quantity and quality, is a pressing issue in East Asian countries. Rapid economic growth in this sub-region has come at considerable environmental cost, including the depletion and pollution of already scarce surface and groundwater resources. Through new and established partnerships - and building on achievements UNESCO category-2 centres - Beijing Office will provide policy advice; develop and support training and capacity development for water managers and professionals in Ecohydrology, IWRM, water education and water and culture towards greater public awareness, understanding and appreciation of water security issues.</narrative>
  </description>
